{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/registry_ingress.j2 -- the first-entry guard's ONE call of the registry ingress
    macro. Bindings (template_vars; reserved names): rh_ri_decl = the absolute path of the ingress declaration,
    rh_ri_root = the repository root (the guard's discovery rule), rh_ri_supplied = the names visible to the play at
    the guard. The import path is the declared macros_rel relative to dirname(the declared entry_rel), so the
    declaration drives it. The ingress declaration is parsed here; the registry is not. Both parses are the DK03
    parse (lme_doc_admit_text) under dp, the document_channel.parse contract carried by the admitted launch record
    (rh_source_bootstrap.context.document_parse, an interface accessor read before any declaration); the macro
    reconciles dp with the registry node after the registry parse.
    op1e HOLE-OP1D-PREPARSE-PARSE-SOURCE (records-route-op1e-01 OP1E-TT-01; codex 918 known_joins.parser_source): the
    early parser settings come from an EXTERNALLY ADMITTED channel only, never from the document being admitted and never
    from a private default: the external X2 admission (rh_x2_admission, the same mapping the macro binds to the actual
    executing entry and registry identity; its document_parse field, a second interface accessor of the same class as
    the envelope one; C1 word OWED-C1-OP1E-X2-BOUNDARY) when it is a mapping, else the launch envelope as before. This
    choice grants nothing: the macro refuses, before any registry capture, unless the X2 admission is supplied exactly
    when the executing entry is the declared projector (and then equals dp field for field), and the registry parse is
    still reconciled with dp after it. -#}
{%- set dp = rh_x2_admission.document_parse if rh_x2_admission is mapping else rh_source_bootstrap.context.document_parse -%}
{%- set d = lookup('ansible.builtin.file', rh_ri_decl) | lme_doc_admit_text(dp, rh_ri_decl | relpath(rh_ri_root)) -%}
{%- import d.macros_rel | relpath(d.entry_rel | dirname) as ri -%}
{{ ri[d.macro](d, rh_ri_root, rh_ri_supplied, dp, rh_source_bootstrap) }}
